course: dictionary
lesson: 8404
title: Words for low sounds
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words sound like what they mean. Say «rumble» out loud and it sounds low and heavy, like the thing it describes. «Thunder rumbles because sound from different parts of the long lightning bolt reaches you at different times.» The sentence tells you rumbles is a long, low sound.
explain: Rumble can be a verb (to rumble) or a noun (a rumble). Look at the words around it to find which one you have. In «Elephants make deep rumbles, many too low for us to hear», the word deep is a clue: a rumble is a low, rolling sound that you may feel more than hear.
explain: Words can also have more than one meaning. Rumble can mean a deep sound, but in UK informal speech it can mean to find out someone's secret or trick. Try each meaning in the sentence. Only one will make sense.
fact: To rumble is to make a long, low, deep sound, like thunder or a big truck.
fact: A rumble is such a low, rolling sound.
fact: «A hungry tummy rumbles» and «thunder rumbles» are both examples of rumbling sounds.
fact: In UK informal speech, to rumble someone means to find out their secret or trick.
fact: A rumble strip on a road makes a car rumble to warn the driver.
exercise: «Thunder rumbles because sound from different parts of the long lightning bolt reaches you at different times.» In this sentence, rumbles means | *makes a long, low, deep sound | jumps high into the air | finds out a secret | shines brightly
exercise: «Hunger shows as a rumbling tummy, low energy, grumpiness and trouble paying attention.» What does rumbling mean here? | very tiny and quiet | *making a low, deep sound | very quick and sudden | sore and painful
exercise: Nadia says, «I will rumble your trick!» What does rumble mean? | *to find out someone's secret or trick | to roll down a hill | to make a deep sound like a truck | to paint a wall
test: Find and copy one word that means a low, deep sound. | ears | trumpet | trunk | *rumbles
test: Why does a rumble strip on a road make a car rumble? | To stop the car quickly | To make the road smoother | *To warn the driver | To light up the road at night
exam: Are «thunder rumbles» and «to rumble someone's trick» the same meaning? | No, both mean to paint | Yes, both mean a loud noise | *No, one is a low sound and the other finds out a secret | Yes, both mean to jump
